    <string name="intro_control_title">You stay in control</string>
    <string name="intro_control_body">Write down a task, choose a first step and start at your own pace. You can pause and return later. Suggestions are calculated on your phone, and you decide what to do with them.</string>
    <string name="intro_duration_title">Reference points from your own durations</string>
    <string name="intro_duration_body">The app measures active time spent on your tasks without counting pauses. After three measured completions, it can suggest a reference duration. You can correct that reference or exclude an unusual measurement.</string>
    <string name="intro_duration_example">8, 11 and 13 minutes → a 14-minute reference.</string>
    <string name="intro_duration_rule">The rule keeps the longest eligible active duration, rounds it up to the next minute, then adds one minute. A manual reference stays in priority.</string>
    <string name="intro_context_title">Suggestions that fit the moment</string>
    <string name="intro_context_body">If you enable it, the app can take your energy, available time and context into account. The die uses eligible tasks only when you ask it to. You stay in control of their order.</string>
    <string name="intro_enable_suggestions">Enable suggestions</string>
